==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|ἔκζεμα|tr=ekzema|lang=grc}}, from {{term|ἐκ|tr=ek||out of, forth from|lang=grc}} + {{term|ζέμα|tr=zema||that which is boiled, decoction|lang=grc}}, from {{term|ζέω|tr=zeo||to boil, to seethe|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|eczemata|pl2=eczemas|-}}

# An acute or chronic [[inflammation]] of the [[skin]], characterized by redness, itching, and the outbreak of oozing [[vesicular]] [[lesion]]s which become encrusted and scaly. It is noncontagious.

====Hypernyms====
* [[dermatitis]]

====Derived terms====
* [[eczematic]]
* [[eczematous ]]

